# nougat.mmd — extraction stub (backfill note)

## Status: NOT RUN — not applicable to this replication

There is **no `paper.pdf` on disk** for this replication.

## Why
The paper (Debreceni et al. 2024, *Toxics* 12(8):545, PMC11359366) is open-access CC-BY and was harvested directly from Europe PMC as JATS XML — a structured, tag-rich source that is strictly better than PDF OCR for downstream text/table extraction. Running Nougat on a re-exported PDF of the same content would strictly LOSE information (equation LaTeX, table structure, reference targets) compared to the JATS XML already staged.

## What was harvested instead

| Path | Source | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `source/fulltext.xml` | Europe PMC `ptpmcrender.fcgi?accid=PMC11359366&blobtype=xml` | JATS XML (structured) |
| `source/fulltext.txt` | Detagged plain text of the above | UTF-8 text |

## If Nougat extraction is ever needed
1. Fetch a PDF: `curl -o paper.pdf "https://europepmc.org/backend/ptpmcrender.fcgi?accid=PMC11359366&blobtype=pdf"`
2. Run: `nougat paper.pdf -o extraction/ -m 0.1.0-base` (or newer)
3. Output would replace this stub with the actual Nougat mmd.

## Free-endpoint note
Any future Nougat run should stay on local CPU/GPU (Nougat is a free open-source model from Meta); no paid API involved.

